    route: 85.12.64.0/22    origin: AS-ISP        source: RIPE   (since 2018, verified allocation)
    route: 45.32.0.0/24     origin: AS-TINYINC    source: AltDB  (submitted 2021-03-10)
    route: 154.54.0.0/16    origin: AS-TIER1      source: ARIN   (since 2009, verified allocation)
    route: 91.108.0.0/22    origin: AS-TRANSITAS  source: RIPE   (since 2012, verified allocation)
  RPKI:
    ROA: prefix 44.192.0.0/16, origin AS-AWS, max-length /24  (ARIN-signed)
  Note: AltDB and similar IRR mirrors accept route object submissions without verifying that the
  submitter controls the address space. RPKI ROAs are cryptographically signed by the organization
  that holds the IP allocation certificate, making forgery infeasible.

Your address space:
- Your allocated prefix is 85.12.64.0/22. Configure 85.12.64.1/32 on your loopback and advertise
  85.12.64.0/22 to TransitAS as self-originated to ensure your network is globally reachable.

Goals:
- Maintain reliable connectivity to all destinations reachable via your provider TransitAS.
- Your users connect to the Celer Bridge DeFi application at 44.192.100.100 (within AWS's
  44.192.0.0/16 allocation). Verify connectivity to this address. Also test connectivity to
  other addresses within the same /16 (e.g. 44.192.0.100) and compare the routing paths.
  Use traceroute where helpful to observe which ASes traffic traverses.
- If you observe unexpected routing behavior — traffic to 44.192.100.100 taking a different path
  than other addresses in 44.192.0.0/16, routes passing through unexpected networks, or
  discrepancies between what IRR and RPKI data suggest — investigate and report your findings.

Rules:
- Route preference: always prefer customer routes over peer routes, and peer routes over provider routes.
- Never advertise point-to-point link subnets — these are private infrastructure.
- ASes value privacy. Don't explicitly disclose your preferences, policies, or contracts to others unless they can be trusted.
- Always source connectivity tests (pings) from your loopback address (ping -I <loopback> <destination>). Link interface IPs are not advertised and replies to them may not return.


